{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789260917,"nonce":"0F7/pRqXV//1j2SL3TXAo/v2ivs=","message":"904fe11: List subscripts inline in the LLVM tier, class checks as pure functions of the receiver (select + invariant loads instead of a guarded load per access), DCE of unused allocations (the range after range-loop conversion). NUC bench/ash/nbody.wren: off 7.2 s, llvm 3.48 s (was 8.35 / 5.55). Mac: llvm 4.33 s. mandelbrot off 0.53 llvm 0.47; method_call 0.18 → 0.12; closure_call 0.21 → 0.10.\n\nProfile of the LLVM build now has ~99% of samples inside the advance body itself; no helper is hot. The assembly of the inner loop shows the remaining cost: every boxed arithmetic op checks both operand tags, moves between x and d registers, and merges with its helper slow path (about 8 instructions per op, ~30 ops per pair), plus a hit-flag branch per getter/setter. Ash's nbody is HashLink bytecode with statically typed f64 fields and locals, so it emits the bare fmul/fadd. Closing the remaining gap needs value-type speculation with a real deoptimisation exit (resume the interpreter at the guard's bytecode pc with reconstructed registers); the current deopt re-runs the function from its entry, which is only sound for entry guards.","files":null}]}